# 1️⃣ Cycle Detection in Directed Graph

Undirected cycle detection uses:

```text
Parent Node
```

But in Directed Graph:

```text
Parent concept fails
```

We use:

```text
Recursion Stack
```

---

## Example

```text
1 → 2
↑   ↓
4 ← 3
```

Cycle:

```text
1 → 2 → 3 → 4 → 1
```

---

# 2️⃣ DFS Recursion Stack Method

Maintain:

```text
visited[]
```

and

```text
pathVisited[]
```

---

### Meaning

```text
visited[node]
```

Node already explored.

---

```text
pathVisited[node]
```

Node currently in DFS path.

---

### Observation

If during DFS:

```text
neighbor already exists
in pathVisited
```

Then:

```text
Cycle Exists
```

---

# 3️⃣ C++ Code

```cpp
bool dfs(
    int node,
    vector<int> adj[],
    vector<int>& vis,
    vector<int>& pathVis)
{
    vis[node] = 1;

    pathVis[node] = 1;

    for(int neighbor : adj[node])
    {
        if(!vis[neighbor])
        {
            if(
                dfs(
                    neighbor,
                    adj,
                    vis,
                    pathVis
                )
            )
            {
                return true;
            }
        }
        else if(pathVis[neighbor])
        {
            return true;
        }
    }

    pathVis[node] = 0;

    return false;
}
```

---

### Complexity

```text
Time: O(V + E)

Space: O(V)
```

