# 4️⃣ Cycle Detection using Kahn's Algorithm

## Idea

Topological Sort works only for:

```text
DAG
```

If graph contains cycle:

```text
Topological Sort
cannot include all nodes.
```

---

### Observation

If:

```text
Topological Nodes Count
<
Total Nodes
```

Then:

```text
Cycle Exists
```

---

# 5️⃣ Kahn's Cycle Detection

```cpp
bool hasCycle(
    int V,
    vector<int> adj[])
{
    vector<int> indegree(
        V,
        0
    );

    for(int i=0;i<V;i++)
    {
        for(int neighbor :
            adj[i])
        {
            indegree[
                neighbor
            ]++;
        }
    }

    queue<int> q;

    for(int i=0;i<V;i++)
    {
        if(indegree[i]==0)
        {
            q.push(i);
        }
    }

    int count = 0;

    while(!q.empty())
    {
        int node = q.front();

        q.pop();

        count++;

        for(int neighbor :
            adj[node])
        {
            indegree[
                neighbor
            ]--;

            if(
                indegree[
                    neighbor
                ] == 0
            )
            {
                q.push(
                    neighbor
                );
            }
        }
    }

    return count != V;
}
```

---

### Complexity

```text
Time: O(V + E)

Space: O(V)
```

