# 🔟 Dijkstra Algorithm

## Purpose

Find shortest path from:

```text
Source Node
```

to:

```text
All Nodes
```

---

### Condition

Works only when:

```text
All Edge Weights
>= 0
```

---

### Example

```text
0 --4--> 1

0 --1--> 2

2 --2--> 1
```

Shortest:

```text
0 → 2 → 1
```

Cost:

```text
3
```

---

# 1️⃣1️⃣ Greedy Idea

Always process:

```text
Closest Unprocessed Node
```

Use:

```text
Min Heap
```

---

# 1️⃣2️⃣ Dijkstra Algorithm Steps

### Step 1

Push:

```text
(source,0)
```

into Min Heap.

---

### Step 2

Take minimum distance node.

---

### Step 3

Relax all edges.

---

### Step 4

Update distances.

---

### Step 5

Push updated distance.

---

# 1️⃣3️⃣ C++ Code

```cpp
vector<int> dijkstra(
    int V,
    vector<vector<int>> adj[],
    int src)
{
    priority_queue<
        pair<int,int>,
        vector<pair<int,int>>,
        greater<pair<int,int>>
    > pq;

    vector<int> dist(
        V,
        1e9
    );

    dist[src] = 0;

    pq.push({0, src});

    while(!pq.empty())
    {
        auto current =
            pq.top();

        pq.pop();

        int dis =
            current.first;

        int node =
            current.second;

        for(auto edge :
            adj[node])
        {
            int adjNode =
                edge[0];

            int wt =
                edge[1];

            if(
                dis + wt
                <
                dist[adjNode]
            )
            {
                dist[adjNode] =
                    dis + wt;

                pq.push({
                    dist[adjNode],
                    adjNode
                });
            }
        }
    }

    return dist;
}
```

---

### Complexity

```text
Time: O(E log V)

Space: O(V)
```

